SUMMARY:MANHATTAN SHORT Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin us for the 29th Annual MANHATTAN SHORT Film Festival\, a 
 worldwide event taking place in over 500 venues across six continents 
 between September 24 and October 4\,2026.\n\nMANHATTAN SHORT is the only 
 event of its kind. The Ten Finalists will screen simultaneously across the 
 world during a one-week period\,with the Best Film and Best Actor awards 
 determined by ballots cast by the audiences in each participating 
 venue.\n\nMANHATTAN SHORT 2026 Finalists:\nSmall Talk (USA)\, Mary is 
 Missing (Ireland)\, Candy Bar (Australia)\, Vultures (South Africa)\, Life 
 Goes On (United Kingdom)\, Hai Davai (Moldova)\, Pickup (Russia)\, 
 Norheimsund (Cuba)\, When the Sea was Calm (Georgia)\, Never Give Up 
 (Mexico).\n\n\nhttps://www.manhattanshort.com/\n\n\n\n\nThursday\, October 
 1\, 6 PM\n\n\n\nFriday\, October 2\, 1 PM\n\n\n\nSunday\, October 4\, 1:30 
 PM\n\n2 hours\, 45 minutes (Intermission at 1:21)\n\nTrailer: 
 https://youtu.be/iOdETuNe6E0?si=39czrCjxf3znychO\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 2
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10341-17021474
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17021474
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Thespaceforart": "https://thespaceforart.com/event/the-space-we-made-exhibit-opening/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:thespaceforart
X-SOURCE:The Space For Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T200000
DTSTAMP:20260917T211835Z
CREATED:20260917T205927Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T211835Z
UID:10409-1790960400-1790971200@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:The Space We Made - Exhibit Opening
DESCRIPTION:The Space We Made\nOpening Reception \nBefore The Space moves to its new home\, we’re taking a look back and celebrating US!  Everyone who has walked through the door over the last 3 years has helped make The Space what it is.  You’ve lent your support\, energy\, and hearts to this cause.  You came together to explore something new\, shared your art and ideas\, witnessed creativity in action\, made space for one another\, bonded with new friends\, and all with laughter\, love and authenticity.  That was and always will be the invitation of The Space:  to come share\, explore and witness the creative spirit.   \nThis last exhibit in this location take a look back at all the shows\, the people\, and the nights that filled this room. The Space We Made is a photo exhibit of everyone and everything that’s happened here\, and the opening reception is a PARTY!! \nFriday\, October 2 · 5–8 PM \nFree and open to all\, but our fundraising drive has kicked off so donations along with your RSVP would go a long way to keeping The Space alive. \nWe also welcome BYOB drinks and snacks to share.  We are all in this together! \nHelp us send this room off right! \nRSVP encouraged so we know how many people to expect. \nIf you have photos of good times and memories at The Space\, we would love to get them in!  Email them to he***@************rt.com. We will keep adding to the exhibit\, and more photos will be taken here over the next few weeks that we can print and add to the wall.  Its a participatory exhibit that will be up for several weeks.
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/the-space-we-made-exhibit-opening/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260917_170044.jpg
END:VEVENT
