SUMMARY:ARTIST TALKBACK: In Discussion with Playwright\, Director & Composer of "Cassandra: An Ongoing Tragedy" - VIRTUAL
DESCRIPTION:Rich with emotional and social relevance\, Mosaic Dance Theater 
 Company’s world premiere production of Cassandra: An Ongoing Tragedy by 
 award-winning playwright Ruth Cantrell\, contrasts Greek myths to horrors 
 of modern day\, depicting the eternal existence of hate\, and exploring the 
 impact of the evils brought forth from Pandora's Box. The stories told in 
 this piece\, related by fictional characters in historical situations\, are 
 presented by a cast of 11\, through live spoken word and dance\, with a 
 commissioned score of original music.\n\nDirected by Morgiana Celeste 
 Varricchio\, with choreography by Samara Adell\, and music by Michael V. 
 Ficocelli.\n\nThis program is made possible by funds from the Essex County 
 Division of Cultural and Historic Affairs\, a partner of the New Jersey 
 State Council on the Arts\, and funding from The Puffin 
 Foundation.\n\nAdult Program | Virtual | Registration Required\nOPEN to 
 all\n\nIt is highly recommended you attend a performance of Cassandra: An 
 Ongoing Tragedy at the First Congregational Church of Montclair. Click here 
 for performance information and seat reservation.\n\nCONTENT WARNING:\nThis 
 production shows graphic images of violence\, including warfare\, 
 bombings\, and their victims\, with intense\, jarring audio of gunfire and 
 explosions. It is intended for mature audiences and those seeking to 
 understand the events. Please take care of your well-being.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
UID:LibCal-10286-17672017
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17672017
END:VEVENT
