SUMMARY:Morning Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Small Things Like These by Claire Keegan\n\nIt is 1985 in a 
 small Irish town. During the weeks leading up to Christmas\, Bill Furlong\, 
 a coal merchant and family man faces into his busiest season. Early one 
 morning\, while delivering an order to the local convent\, Bill makes a 
 discovery which forces him to confront both his past and the complicit 
 silences of a town controlled by the church.\n\n
