BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_racioppi
SUMMARY:Parish Hike and Potluck
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T130000
DTSTAMP:20260919T042220Z
UID:7v05dden21qqckdksm3juqbk5a@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T090000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260903T133631Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Join us for abeautiful hike to Tripod Rock\, located 
 at the Pyramid Mountain Natural HistoricArea in Montville. We will <b>meet
  at the church parking lot at 8:45am</b> tocaravan or carpool to the trail
 head. The hike should take about 2 1/2 hours.</span></p><p></p><p><b><span
 >Wear sturdyshoes and bring water</span></b><span>\,snacks\, and hiking po
 les (if you have them). Dogs are welcome on the trails butmust be kept on 
 leash at all times. Potluck at Church after hike!</span></p><p></p><p><b><
 u><span>MOREINFORMATION ABOUT THE PARISH HIKE</span></u></b><b><span>:</sp
 an></b><b></b></p><p><span>The 3-mile loophike begins with a 300 foot clim
 b along the Blue Trail\, where we will berewarded with an unobstructed vie
 w of the New York City skyline. (It's a prettysteep climb\, but once we ge
 t to the top it's mostly flat.) We will continue onthe Blue trail to the B
 lue Dot trail which leads to a unique glacial erraticknown as Tripod Rock.
  This renowned\, multi-ton boulder is balanced on threesmall boulders\, an
 d was deposited by the Wisconsin Glacier over 18\,000 years ago.We will th
 en backtrack to the Blue Trail\, descend another steep climb and walkalong
 side the Taylortown Reservoir.  </span></p><p><span>For over 10\,000 year
 s\, this wildernessland provided shelter and served as a hunting\, fishing
 \, and gathering site forthe <b>Lenape Indians</b>\, who may have used Tri
 pod Rock as a celestialcalendar. Later\, notorious outlaws used the region
  as a hide-out\, while 19thcentury explorers and traders came and went.  
 </span></p><p><span>At theconclusion of the hike (which is rated "Moderate
 ") we can check outthe visitor’s center which features Indian artifacts 
 and other exhibits. Joinfor potluck at the Church after that!</span></p><p
 ><span><b>Sign-up in theFellowship Hall</b> or email Father Jerry at <u>re
 ctor@holyspiritverona</u>. <i>Questions?</i><b>See parishioner Ruth Portel
 a</b>.</span></p><p><span> </span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T133631Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Church of the Holy Spirit Verona
END:VEVENT
